{"id":"chatcmpl-63e59f34-071d-49c4-9bca-e311a29de100","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245822,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-tool corroboration strategy for medical image interpretation: an expert model provides a primary read, an independent grounded report cross-checks it, and phrase grounding localizes the finding to a specific region. The pattern generalizes to any visual question-answering task where a single model's judgment should be verified by complementary evidence sources before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Use a domain-expert model first to obtain a primary interpretation, then corroborate with an independent second source before answering.\",\n    \"Apply spatial grounding (localization) to verify that a claimed finding actually appears in the expected anatomical region.\",\n    \"When options are mutually exclusive binary findings (left vs. right), explicitly ask the expert to compare both sides rather than confirm a single hypothesis.\",\n    \"Chain heterogeneous tools (expert read → grounded report → phrase localization) so each contributes distinct evidence, then synthesize into a final answer with justification.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Start with an expert interpretation that compares both candidate findings; corroborate with an independent report; localize the winning finding spatially before answering.\",\n    \"Binary visual discrimination\": \"Frame the expert query as a comparison between the two options rather than a yes/no confirmation, to avoid confirmation bias.\",\n    \"Multi-tool evidence synthesis\": \"Assign each tool a distinct role (primary read, cross-check, localization) and require agreement before finalizing; cite the converging evidence in the answer rationale.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the primary expert read and the independent corroborating source agree on the same finding.\",\n    \"Verify the phrase-grounding localization matches the expected anatomical region for the chosen option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":503,"total_tokens":865,"completion_tokens":362,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":503},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":362}}}